{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Elohim's anger was kindled because he was going.</b> And even though He had given him permission, nevertheless the intent of Balaam the wicked was evident from his actions — for had his intention not been to curse, he would not have gone. Rather, certainly this was his reasoning: since the Holy One, blessed be He, initially told him 'do not go,' and afterward told him 'go' — He must have changed His mind, and his intention was to curse them. Therefore the anger of the Holy One, blessed be He, was kindled, for it should have entered his mind that the Holy One, blessed be He, does not retract His word. And when He said to him 'arise, go with them,' He did not permit him to curse them, but rather, because He saw that he coveted money, He said to him 'go with them' — and he went with intent to curse. Therefore He sent him an angel to be an adversary to him, to make known that He knows his thoughts."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:59.848441320Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}